+{
+  "file": "src/agents.ts",
+  "snippet": "maxDelegations: 0, historyLength: 4 })",
+  "cause": "The triage agent's agents() middleware is configured with maxDelegations: 0, so every delegate_to_* call returns \"Delegation limit reached (0)\" and triage replies without ever reaching orderAgent or refundAgent.",
+  "evidence": "Before the fix, running tryTriage on \"Where is order A-1003?\" returned \"My delegation limit has been reached, and I'm unable to check the status of order A-1003\"; after changing the cap to 2 the same run returned the status (delivered), ETA 2026-10-18 and tracking NW-5D1MZT. The middleware (node_modules/@genkit-ai/middleware/lib/agents.js, ~line 141) rejects a delegation when delegationCount >= maxDelegations, which is 0 >= 0 on the first call. orderAgent is not behind this middleware, which is why it answers correctly on its own."
+}
